## Review — Codex Prime
Date: 2026-10-27.
Disposition: HELD FOR RC-01 REPAIR; NO REAL RETURN-BAND ROLLOUT.
Prime verified all 37 custody rows and reran 23 tests in a disposable copy:22 pass,
one symlink privilege skip. The copied test's hard-coded REAL_BOOK was redirected
to an actual disposable Git workbook; no test was permitted to allocate in the
shared workbook. Original test bytes are preserved. The suite passes its stated
tests, but its Git prohibition is itself the functional mismatch.

RC-01 — reserve/capture refuse every book inside a Git working tree. Prime's
fresh-process probe on a disposable Git workbook exits2 with "book is inside a
Git working tree", creates no member, and reproduces the block. This contradicts
the target: local drops under D:/Git/lib-build's 0100 band before Git publication.
The external-store policy belongs to the separate Clerk job-store experiment;
it must not prevent this archive from being recorded in our local checkout.
Related blanket guards also reject source-root/book overlap and any return file
inside the book. Explicitly selected originating work-page returns/evidence must
be readable without an invented external copy step. Forbid capture of the actual
destination/self aliases; do not forbid the entire workspace as a source root.

RC-02 — the original regression references the real shared workbook directly.
Replace it with disposable regular Git and .git-file worktree fixtures in the
repair. Tests must prove the intended local-checkout path, not merely an external
book copied into Git later. Current publication demo does not establish that path.

Furniture edits and discovery.patch are retained as proposed repair work. Prime
has not applied its stale01.015 target or created0101/0102. A receipt is not review,
publication or acceptance. Next:05.02 fixes the placement contract and tests.
Evidence: evidence/prime-review05.01/ with exact refusal and instrumented-test notes.
